@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# ATTa v121.3.1: fixes for ATTa failures found by the live fleet run
+
+Each change below comes from a real failure on the live server, in fleet run `fleet-20260929T061331Z-9b37b3`
+(29 apps in parallel inside the Coolify-managed ATTa, on EC2 `i-0f13b8644b215931d`).
+
+| # | Real failure (evidence) | ATTa component | Change |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | memos (and super-productivity) failed stage 6 with `CONSOLE_ERRORS`. All 19 errors and all 19 failed requests for memos are `net::ERR_NETWORK_CHANGED` on its own `127.0.0.1:8185` assets, at 06:15:24 while Docker was creating networks for about 20 apps at once. Evidence: `state/runner/evidence/memos/run-1790662411421-memos-e2b8ce1d-a1/browser.json`. Memos passed stage 6 on the earlier run. | `system_watcher.browser_check` (shared stage 6 under parallel load) | When the host's network changes under a page load, the watcher keeps that capture, waits `APP_BUILDER_NET_SETTLE` seconds and loads the page once more. A second interruption gives `BROWSER_NETWORK_CHANGED`, which counts as INCONCLUSIVE (environment), never as an app failure. |
+| 2 | A qualified app never reaches Coolify when another app in the same build fails. v120 handed off only fully QUALIFIED builds, and this run is PARTIALLY_QUALIFIED. | `coolify_handoff`, `pipeline._record_qualification` | Each app that is itself QUALIFIED under the v121.2+ barrier is handed off, including from a PARTIALLY_QUALIFIED build. Apps that did not qualify, and older records without a barrier state, never are. |
+| 3 | The handoff stopped at "Coolify accepted the deploy call" (ACCEPTED / DISPATCHED). Nothing checked that the service ran, that it was reachable, or that it passed stage 6 live. | new `coolify_live.py`, called from the pipeline loop | Each handed-off app goes DISPATCHED → DEPLOYING → RUNNING → VERIFIED, or LIVE_FAILED with evidence. The steps: Coolify's own service status, the service's real containers all running, the Coolify address answering HTTP, then the six-stage watcher with stage 6 in real Chromium against the live address. Every observation is recorded in `state/coolify/live/<app>/<build>/`. |
+| 4 | Re-checking the apps affected by an ATTa fix meant re-running all 29. | `pipeline.process` | `inbox/<id>.library.json` containing `{"only": [apps]}` re-checks just those apps; every other app keeps its result from the latest library build. |
